# The `hchain` input of JL §5, as a named hypothesis

`Work.ORLyndon.magnus_torTwoVanishes` consumes, besides `hA` and `hswap`, the dimension-shifting
equivalence of JL Lemma 5.2

`IsZero (Tor₂^{K[G]}(S, M)) ↔ Tor1Vanishes K[G] (S ⊗_K I_{K[G]}) M` for every left `K[G]`-module `M`,

with `S ⊗_K I_{K[G]}` carrying the canonical diagonal right structure
`Work.ORFlatness.diagRightModule` and `I_{K[G]}` the augmentation ideal.  This file names that
hypothesis so that the assembly of Theorem 1.1 can carry it as a single readable input.

Two forms are needed, because two `Ideal (K[G])` definitions of the augmentation ideal occur in the
workspace:

* `Work.ORFinal.ChainHypFP2` — with `Work.ORFP2.augIdeal K G` (the ideal generated by the
  `single g 1 - 1`).  This is the form produced by the delegated node
  `Work.ORFinal.Chain.chainOfJL52` (`Submission/Work/ORFinal/Chain/`), and
  `Work.ORFinal.ChainInputFP2` is its `∀`-form.
* `Work.ORFinal.ChainHyp` — with `Work.ORLyndon.augIdeal K G` (the kernel of the augmentation,
  the definition used by the paper), which is the form consumed by
  `Work.ORLyndon.magnus_torTwoVanishes`.  `Work.ORFinal.ChainInput` is its `∀`-form, and it is the
  input of the T7 assembly `Work.ORFinal.RealTorInput_of_chainInput`.

The two ideals are equal (both are the kernel of the augmentation, `Work.ORFP2.mem_augIdeal_iff` and
`Work.ORFlatness.augIdeal_eq_ker_augmentation`), so the two forms are equivalent:
`Work.ORFinal.chainHyp_of_augIdeal` transfers the chain across the equality.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ORCoherence.Tor
import Submission.Work.ORFlatness.Flat
import Submission.Work.ORFlatness.DiagonalRight
import Submission.Work.ORFP2.Basic
import Submission.Work.ORLyndon.Augmentation

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

universe u

namespace Work.ORFinal

/-- **The dimension-shifting hypothesis of JL Lemma 5.2**, in the form produced by
`Work.ORFinal.Chain.chainOfJL52`: for a `K`-algebra `S` with structure map `φ : K[G] →ₐ[K] S` and
the canonical diagonal right action on `S ⊗_K I_{K[G]}`, where `I_{K[G]}` is
`Work.ORFP2.augIdeal K G`. -/
def ChainHypFP2 (K : Type u) [Field K] (G : Type u) [Group G] (S : Type u) [Ring S] [Algebra K S]
    (φ : MonoidAlgebra K G →ₐ[K] S) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORFlatness.diagRightModule K G S φ ↥(Work.ORFP2.augIdeal K G)
  ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} (MonoidAlgebra K G)),
    CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero (Work.ORCoherence.Tor φ.toRingHom 2 M) ↔
      Work.ORFlatness.Tor1Vanishes (MonoidAlgebra K G)
        (TensorProduct K S ↥(Work.ORFP2.augIdeal K G)) (↥M)

/-- **The dimension-shifting hypothesis of JL Lemma 5.2**, in the vocabulary of
`Work.ORLyndon.magnus_torTwoVanishes`: the augmentation ideal is `Work.ORLyndon.augIdeal K G`, the
kernel of the augmentation map. -/
def ChainHyp (K : Type u) [Field K] (G : Type u) [Group G] (S : Type u) [Ring S] [Algebra K S]
    (φ : MonoidAlgebra K G →ₐ[K] S) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORFlatness.diagRightModule K G S φ ↥(Work.ORLyndon.augIdeal K G)
  ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} (MonoidAlgebra K G)),
    CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero (Work.ORCoherence.Tor φ.toRingHom 2 M) ↔
      Work.ORFlatness.Tor1Vanishes (MonoidAlgebra K G)
        (TensorProduct K S ↥(Work.ORLyndon.augIdeal K G)) (↥M)

/-- The `Work.ORFP2.augIdeal` form of the chain, for every `K`-algebra `S` with a structure map
`φ : K[G] →ₐ[K] S`: exactly the conclusion of the delegated node
`Work.ORFinal.Chain.chainOfJL52`. -/
def ChainInputFP2 : Prop :=
  ∀ (K : Type) [Field K] (G : Type) [Group G] (S : Type) [Ring S] [Algebra K S]
    (φ : MonoidAlgebra K G →ₐ[K] S), ChainHypFP2 K G S φ

/-- **The dimension-shifting chain of JL Lemma 5.2, in the form the final assembly consumes**: the
`Work.ORLyndon.augIdeal` form for every `K`-algebra `S` with a structure map `φ : K[G] →ₐ[K] S`.

This is the single remaining input of the T7 assembly
(`Work.ORFinal.RealTorInput_of_chainInput`); once `Work.ORFinal.Chain.chainOfJL52` (T6) and the
transfer `Work.ORFinal.chainInput_of_chainInputFP2` have landed it is a theorem. -/
def ChainInput : Prop :=
  ∀ (K : Type) [Field K] (G : Type) [Group G] (S : Type) [Ring S] [Algebra K S]
    (φ : MonoidAlgebra K G →ₐ[K] S), ChainHyp K G S φ

end Work.ORFinal
